@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] authorization-system-actor-origin
SystemActor MUST be created only by trusted in-process coordinators and jobs.
HTTP parameters, socket payloads and claimed user roles MUST NOT be converted
into a SystemActor; external host credentials require separate authentication.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] authorization-explicit-action-access
Adding an Ash action MUST NOT implicitly authorize it. Public entry actions need
explicit admission and fresh record-specific checks in their coordinators;
internal actions require both the resource/action allowlist and Cedar permission.
